From 5d9f290af8effdeffd7579c08c13ce98aa4702a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:09:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Register the service worker with an update banner, and open
 maps in the map app

The Angular service worker was being built (angular.json) but nothing ever
registered it, so the installed app got no caching and no updates. It's
now registered immediately in production, with an AppUpdateService that
checks for new deploys on launch, every 30 minutes and whenever the app
comes back into view, and a banner above the page that offers a one-tap
reload. Hosting serves the worker, its manifest and index.html uncached
and hashed bundles as immutable, the worker never hijacks the standalone
/maps page, and the manifest gets an id, scope and root start URL.

Opening an address from the installed app used an https Google Maps link,
which opens an in-app browser sheet that the OS then hands to the Maps app,
leaving a blank white sheet to come back to. Directions and places now go
through the map apps' own URL schemes on phones (Google Maps, then Apple
Maps on iOS; Google Maps on Android), falling back to the web link when no
app answers, and open the web in a new tab on desktop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YT3ubrcTis7ctkWAXDLv49
